---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy · My Family Allowance">
  <Fragment slot="nav">
    <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" href="/">Home</a>
  </Fragment>

  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: August 31, 2026</p>

    <p>
      My Family Allowance is a small family money tracker. This page explains what
      information the app stores and how it is used.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      When you sign in with Google, we receive your Google account name and email
      address. We use that to create and identify your parent account.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use the app, we also store the family data you enter: kids’ names,
      allowance amounts, balances, transaction memos, your family page URL slug,
      and the shared family password hash.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We use this information only to run the service: keep you signed in, show
      your family’s balances, and credit weekly allowance on schedule. We do not
      sell personal data or use it for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and sessions</h2>
    <p>
      After Google login, we set a secure session cookie so you stay signed in as
      a parent. On the family page, a separate cookie remembers that someone
      entered the family password correctly (for about seven days).
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see family data</h2>
    <p>
      Parents who sign in see their own family’s admin data. Anyone with the
      family URL and password can see that family’s kid totals and history. Keep
      the family link and password private.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Sign-in is handled by Google. Hosting and the database run on Netlify. Those
      providers process data as needed to deliver their services under their own
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Data stays in the database while your account and family records exist. If
      you want your account or family data removed, contact the site operator
      using the link in the footer on the home page.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Kids may view balances on the shared family page. Parents control what is
      entered and who gets the family password. The app is meant for parents to
      manage allowance for their own children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes in a meaningful way, the date at the top of this page
      will be updated.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
